# Retire policy 2026-11-20: production ended 2024; retire dates are road-presence estimates, staggered by colourway.
# BMW 1-series F40 five-door hatchback, 2019-2024.
#
# The third 1-series: the front-wheel-drive UKL2 car, five-door only, with
# the short bonnet, the large kidney grille and the transverse engine. UK
# ordering opened 28 May 2019, first deliveries September 2019.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_1_Series_(F40)
#
# Dimensions 4.319 x 1.799 x 1.434 m, wheelbase 2.670 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show the five-door in side, front and
# rear views; the side view governs.
#
# Colours: grade (c), names evidenced for the F40: Alpine White, Jet Black,
# Misano Blue and Melbourne Red. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 225 km/h. Comfort 85/458, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 85. Classes 1,2.
# Dates are road presence: 2019 intro, retires staggered 2034-2037.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-f40.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-1-series-f40.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-1-series-f40/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the Sport bumper openings and rear lamp contours are
# simplified, and the M135i show car's M trim was not copied. At 128 px the
# short-bonnet front-drive five-door shell and large grille read as an F40.


obj=citycar
name=BMW1SeriesF40(AlpineWhite)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
intro_year=2019
intro_month=9
retire_year=2034
retire_month=6
speed=225
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=85
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=458

